   "description": "Where on the earth this node is, in decimal degrees. Optional, and a node without it is in no way less real \u2014 most trees will be filled in from the top down over months, and a great many nodes will never have one. What it buys is that anything counted per node can be drawn on a map: a product asks the geo adapter for a node's point and gets one or None, rather than keeping its own second list of where places are. Both values or neither; a Float left empty stores as 0.0, so half a pair would be drawn confidently in the Gulf of Guinea.",
